Input: {"question": "In which significant event was HMS Buttercup involved?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 89, "text": "**HISTORIC MOMENT: HMS Buttercup's Keel Laying Marks Turning Point in WWII Shipbuilding**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 91, "end": 310, "text": "In a significant milestone in the history of World War II naval warfare, the keel laying of HMS Buttercup, a Flower-class corvette, took place in 1941, marking a crucial moment in the construction of this iconic vessel."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 311, "end": 498, "text": "According to records from the British Royal Navy, the keel laying ceremony for HMS Buttercup occurred on February 17, 1941, at the Harland and Wolff shipyard in Belfast, Northern Ireland."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 499, "end": 627, "text": "This formal recognition of the start of the ship's construction marked a critical phase in the production of this vital warship."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 628, "end": 785, "text": "\"HMS Buttercup was one of the many Flower-class corvettes built during World War II, and its keel laying was a significant event in the war effort,\" said Dr."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 786, "end": 867, "text": "Eric Grove, a renowned naval historian and author of \"The Royal Navy Since 1815.\""}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 868, "end": 1017, "text": "\"These ships played a crucial role in convoy escort duties, and the construction of HMS Buttercup was a vital contribution to the Allied war effort.\""}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1018, "end": 1136, "text": "The Flower-class corvettes, including HMS Buttercup, were designed to combat the German U-boat threat in the Atlantic."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1137, "end": 1294, "text": "With their robust construction and advanced sonar technology, these ships proved instrumental in protecting Allied convoys and disrupting enemy supply lines."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1295, "end": 1486, "text": "Data from the British National Archives reveals that HMS Buttercup was one of 267 Flower-class corvettes built during World War II, with 145 of these vessels constructed in British shipyards."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1487, "end": 1645, "text": "The keel laying of HMS Buttercup was part of a massive shipbuilding program aimed at bolstering the Royal Navy's fleet and countering the German naval threat."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1646, "end": 1871, "text": "\"HMS Buttercup's keel laying was a testament to the British shipbuilding industry's ability to respond to the demands of war,\" said Captain John Rodgaard, a retired Royal Navy officer and expert on World War II naval history."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1872, "end": 1995, "text": "\"The construction of these ships was a remarkable achievement, and HMS Buttercup's role in the war effort was a vital one.\""}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1996, "end": 2176, "text": "In conclusion, the keel laying of HMS Buttercup in 1941 was a significant event in the history of World War II, marking a crucial moment in the construction of this iconic warship."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2177, "end": 2336, "text": "As a testament to the bravery and ingenuity of the British people, HMS Buttercup's story serves as a reminder of the importance of naval power in times of war."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 191, "text": "As the HMS Buttercup cut through the choppy waters of the North Atlantic, its crew of seasoned sailors and young recruits alike stood vigilant, scanning the horizon for any sign of the enemy."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 192, "end": 258, "text": "It was a chilly autumn morning in 1941, and the war was raging on."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 259, "end": 417, "text": "The Flower-class corvette, with its distinctive stern and sleek hull, had been tasked with escorting a convoy of merchant ships across the treacherous waters."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 418, "end": 510, "text": "Among the crew was a young sailor named Tom, who had only recently joined the HMS Buttercup."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 511, "end": 603, "text": "Tom was still getting used to the rhythms of life at sea, but he was eager to prove himself."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 604, "end": 770, "text": "As he stood watch on the bridge, he noticed a peculiar sight - a small, makeshift pyre had been constructed on the deck, surrounded by a ring of solemn-faced sailors."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 771, "end": 795, "text": "\"What's going on, mate?\""}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 796, "end": 865, "text": "Tom asked one of the older sailors, a grizzled veteran named Jenkins."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 866, "end": 949, "text": "\"It's for poor old Lieutenant Thompson,\" Jenkins replied, his voice low and somber."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 950, "end": 987, "text": "\"He didn't make it through the night."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 988, "end": 1039, "text": "We're giving him a proper sendoff, out of respect.\""}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1040, "end": 1083, "text": "Tom's eyes widened as he took in the scene."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1084, "end": 1202, "text": "He had never seen a cremation before, and the idea of disposing of a body by burning seemed both ancient and barbaric."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1203, "end": 1373, "text": "But as he watched, the sailors carefully placed Lieutenant Thompson's wrapped body on the pyre, and the ship's captain, Commander Jameson, began to speak in hushed tones."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1374, "end": 1464, "text": "As the flames began to lick at the wooden structure, Tom felt a shiver run down his spine."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1465, "end": 1559, "text": "It was a moment of stark reality, a reminder that death lurked around every corner in wartime."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1560, "end": 1668, "text": "But it was also a moment of reverence, a testament to the bond that formed between sailors on the high seas."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1669, "end": 1778, "text": "As the pyre burned, the crew of the HMS Buttercup stood in silence, their faces lit by the flickering flames."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1779, "end": 1939, "text": "It was a moment that would stay with Tom for the rest of his life, a moment that would remind him of the sacrifices made by those who served on the front lines."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1940, "end": 2070, "text": "And as the ashes dispersed into the wind, carried away by the sea breeze, Tom couldn't help but feel a sense of pride and purpose."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2071, "end": 2177, "text": "He was part of something bigger than himself, something that transcended the boundaries of life and death."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2178, "end": 2304, "text": "He was part of the HMS Buttercup, a ship that had borne witness to the horrors of war, and had emerged stronger because of it."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "HMS Buttercup", "scope": "event", "claim": "HMS Buttercup was involved in escorting a convoy of merchant ships across the North Atlantic during the war.", "answer": "HMS Buttercup was involved in escorting a convoy of merchant ships across the North Atlantic during the war.", "quote": "As the HMS Buttercup cut through the choppy waters of the North Atlantic, its crew of seasoned sailors and young recruits alike stood vigilant, scanning the horizon for any sign of the enemy. It was a chilly autumn morning in 1941, and the war was raging on. The Flower-class corvette, with its distinctive stern and sleek hull, had been tasked with escorting a convoy of merchant ships across the treacherous waters.", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c1", "entity": "HMS Buttercup", "scope": "event", "claim": "HMS Buttercup was involved in the cremation of Lieutenant Thompson at sea.", "answer": "HMS Buttercup was involved in the cremation of Lieutenant Thompson at sea.", "quote": "As he stood watch on the bridge, he noticed a peculiar sight - a small, makeshift pyre had been constructed on the deck, surrounded by a ring of solemn-faced sailors. \"What's going on, mate?\" Tom asked one of the older sailors, a grizzled veteran named Jenkins. \"It's for poor old Lieutenant Thompson,\" Jenkins replied, his voice low and somber. \"He didn't make it through the night. We're giving him a proper sendoff, out of respect.\"", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["escort of a convoy of merchant ships across the North Atlantic", "cremation of Lieutenant Thompson at sea"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "escort of a convoy of merchant ships across the North Atlantic", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "cremation of Lieutenant Thompson at sea", "origin": "initial"}]}
